            "expect": {
                "CType": "camino_textmedia_teaser_grid",
                "header": "The Main Camino Routes",
                "bodytext": "<p>The Camino de Compostela is a network of ancient pilgrimage routes, each leading to the Cathedral of Santiago de Compostela. Whether crossing mountain passes, following coastal paths, or winding through rolling countryside, every route has its own character and charm — yet all share the same spirit of community, discovery, and adventure.</p>",
                "tx_themecamino_link_label": "Compare all routes"
            },
            "set": {
                "header": "The main Camino routes",
                "bodytext": "<p>Every route ends at the Cathedral of Santiago de Compostela. Some cross mountain passes, some follow the coast and some run through open farmland.</p>",
