                "link_label": "More",
                "text": "The Camino Primitivo is the oldest of all the Camino routes, tracing the original path walked by pilgrims centuries ago. Shorter than the Camino Francés but more physically demanding, it winds through the mountains and forests of Asturias and Galicia. It is a rewarding choice for experienced walkers who prefer solitude and a deeper sense of history along the way."
